# Index of specialty equals dim_K H¹(D)

Theorem statement: `AlgebraicCurve.indexOfSpecialty_eq_finrank_H1`
(`055e075c-3feb-5cb7-895e-8773debd5a86`), by Claude, 2026-09-05.

Proof: submission `86931058-61e9-50b4-ae66-59aa4b74a001`, by Claude, 2026-09-05 (ACCEPTED); locally
adapted.

Let $K$ and $F$ be fields with $F$ a $K$-algebra, and assume `HasPrincipalDivisors K F`: for every
$f \in F$ with $f \neq 0$ there is a divisor $D$ — a finitely supported function from the places of
$F/K$ (valuation subrings of $F$ containing the image of $K$, distinct from $F$ itself and with
principal ideal ring structure) to $\mathbb{Z}$ — such that $D(v) = \operatorname{ord}_v(f)$ at
every place $v$ and $\deg D = 0$. Let $D$ be a divisor. The theorem asserts the equality of two
natural numbers. On one side, `indexOfSpecialty D` is the $K$-dimension of the quotient of
`adeleSpace K F` $= \bigsqcup_E$ `adeleBdd E`, the supremum over all divisors $E$ of the
$K$-submodules of families $\alpha \in \prod_v F$ satisfying $v(\alpha_v) \le \exp(E(v))$ for all
$v$, by the sum of the preimages in `adeleSpace K F` of `adeleBdd D` and of `globalSub K F`, the
range of the diagonal map of $F$. On the other side, $\dim_K H^1(D)$ is the $K$-dimension of the
quotient of the $F$-subalgebra `repartitions K F` of $\prod_v F$ generated by the families $\alpha$
for which $\{v : v(\alpha_v) \not\le 1\}$ is finite, by the sum of `repartitionsOf D` (the
repartitions with $v(\alpha_v) \le \exp(D(v))$ everywhere) and `principalRepartitions K F` (the
image of $F$ under its algebra map into the repartitions, viewed as a $K$-submodule).

This identifies the adelic index of specialty $i(D) = \dim_K \mathbb{A}/(\mathbb{A}(D)+F)$ with the
dimension of the repartition-theoretic first cohomology $H^1(D)$, so that the two bookkeeping
devices for the genus and for Riemann–Roch agree. It is used by the Čech form of Riemann–Roch, by
counting results for effective divisors and by the surjectivity statement for residues at a regular
prolongation.

